# Template for packages/mobile/.env — copy to `.env` and fill in real values.
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY in this file. `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is not.
#
# Metro INLINES every EXPO_PUBLIC_* reference as a string literal at BUNDLE time,
# so these are compile-time constants in the shipped JS — not a runtime lookup.
# Two consequences:
#   1. Changing a value requires restarting the dev server (`--clear` to be sure);
#      a running bundler will keep serving the old literal.
#   2. Anything here is READABLE in the shipped bundle. Only public-by-design values
#      belong in EXPO_PUBLIC_*. Never put a service_role key or any secret here.
#
# All three are public by design: the anon key grants nothing on its own (every
# tenant table is RLS FORCE default-deny and needs a verified user JWT).
#
# If a value is MISSING: a dev build falls back to an obviously-fake
# `.supabase.invalid` placeholder and logs a `config.dev_placeholder_used` warning,
# so the app still boots with no backend provisioned. A RELEASE build THROWS at
# startup instead — see src/api/config.ts.

# Base URL of the Supabase project.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# The project's public anon key (the long `eyJ...` JWT from the API settings page).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Base URL the Edge Functions are served under. Route names are appended to this.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co/functions/v1

# ─── Account-screen destinations (src/config/legalLinks.ts) ──────────────────
# Each row on the "Help & legal" section self-HIDES until its value is a real
# destination — a hidden row is strictly better at App Store review than one that
# opens a 404, so leaving these unset ships an honest (smaller) screen.
#
# HARD App Store requirement for a subscription app (Guideline 3.1.2): both a
# Privacy Policy AND a Terms of Use link must be reachable in-app. Host
# docs/legal/privacy-policy.md and docs/legal/terms-of-service.md at public https
# URLs, then set these. Only an `https://` value is accepted (http / placeholder → hidden).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=https://your-domain.example/privacy
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TERMS_OF_USE_URL=https://your-domain.example/terms

# Support contact (NOT an Apple requirement — Apple's Support URL is a listing field —
# but the published privacy policy promises users a contact for data-rights requests,
# tracked as TBC-05 in docs/legal/README.md). Set EITHER an email (rendered as a
# mailto: that opens the composer, PREFERRED since the policy promises an email) OR a
# hosted https help page. A non-email / http / placeholder value is treated as unset.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@your-domain.example
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_URL=https://your-domain.example/help
